# Copy to ~/.config/linux-cleaner/env (see RUNBOOK.md systemd section).
# Safe-tier defaults for systemd EnvironmentFile=-
# linux-cleaner-clean.service passes only --clean --force, so LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH
# and LINUX_CLEANER_RISK in this file apply to the timer.
LINUX_CLEANER_FORCE=1
# Enabling LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH makes the daily timer quarantine instead of delete.
# Set LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH_KEEP_DAYS (or enable linux-cleaner-retention.timer) to
# purge old quarantine sessions automatically.
# LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH=1
# LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH_KEEP_DAYS=30
LINUX_CLEANER_RISK=safe
# Optional bounded contention wait; literal decimal 0..2147483647 seconds.
# Unset/empty/0 fails fast; positive requires flock. CLI --lock-wait overrides.
# LINUX_CLEANER_LOCK_WAIT=30
# Raising LINUX_CLEANER_RISK above safe makes the unattended deletion of medium
# targets (for example package caches) irreversible. C++ build rows are safe.
# LINUX_CLEANER_QUIET=1
# LINUX_CLEANER_DEBUG=1
# Send a desktop notification summarizing the cleanup result, or a critical notice when the run stops early with an error (requires notify-send).
# LINUX_CLEANER_NOTIFY=1
# Use an absolute config path here: EnvironmentFile does not expand $HOME,
# and the cleaner uses LINUX_CLEANER_CONFIG literally. Unset uses normal discovery.
# LINUX_CLEANER_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/cleaner.conf
# LINUX_CLEANER_ONLY_TARGET=NPM
# LINUX_CLEANER_EXCLUDE_TARGET=Chromium
# Select one existing project using a literal absolute path (no $HOME/tilde/globs).
# CLI --only-path overrides; unset/empty means no scope. Excludes action:* rows.
# Do not combine with LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH_KEEP_DAYS; use the retention timer instead.
# LINUX_CLEANER_ONLY_PATH="/absolute/project path"
# Skip the daily cleanup when the planned reclaimable total is below this size.
# LINUX_CLEANER_MIN_RECLAIM=500M
# Raise every ordinary target's age threshold to at least this many days; skips action:* rows.
# LINUX_CLEANER_MIN_AGE=14
# LINUX_CLEANER_LOG=$HOME/.cache/linux-cleaner/ops.log
# JSON is for dry-run, inventory and --report only; leave unset for the cleanup service.
# Use linux-cleaner-monitor.service for scheduled JSON previews.
# LINUX_CLEANER_EXCLUDE=.git,*.log
# LINUX_CLEANER_ALLOW_OUTSIDE_HOME is deprecated and ignored. Targets outside
# HOME are always allowed. Package-cache rows stay medium risk, so they still
# need LINUX_CLEANER_RISK=medium; under RISK=safe they are not selected.
# Never schedule by default — danger-tier bypass.
# LINUX_CLEANER_YES_DANGER=1
# Retention age is set in examples/systemd/linux-cleaner-retention.service (older-than:30).
